# K03 NS-ROLES-2 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-2-20261007-20; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #declaration-visibility): a named Structure's body takes the common roles of the root and a method.
# In Host's nested Inner, `me: Inner` binds me to Inner itself -- a nested Structure is visible in its own body (below
# its place): a write through Host\Inner\me reaches Inner's own k.  Exit 7; 81 if me held a copy.
Host:
    (): Inner
        int: k 1
        me: Inner
    end: Inner
end: Host
fn: m () int
    Host\Inner\me\k: 4
    if: Host\Inner\k != 4
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
